{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFourteen test files hand-build a nested pytest invocation (`[sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", ...]`),\nand two more deliberately spawn the BARE `pytest` console script. The `--basetemp` family arrived as\nthree separate closed bugs — `grindable-deviant-angwantibo` (`bf7c-333e-29b0-4ee4`, closed) repaired\n`tests/_store_isolation.py:33-50` after its RCA pinned pytest session-finish `cleanup_numbered_dir`\nas the liveness owner; `acidic-ferreous-mole` (`444d-62ff-2c3c-42a9`, closed) repaired the parity\ncollection child now at `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:839-856`; `asbestos-popular-tench`\n(`fb03-2609-ef83-4b41`, closed) inventoried every launch site and repaired the two remaining\nexecuting children in `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py` and `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py`.\nSession log `kilted-centauric-cardinal` (`0bd6-4729-e79e-433b`) root-caused the shutdown timeout.\n\nAll three are fixed. What survives is the duplication that made them arrive as three instalments:\nfourteen independently hand-assembled argv lists, each re-deciding basetemp, timeout, cache plugin\nand stdin. Three still carry no `--basetemp` today — `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py:25`\n(which EXECUTES three real integration nodes and is therefore a live instance of the same defect,\nmissed by the asbestos inventory because it is `pytest.mark.integration`), and the two `--collect-only`\nchildren at `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:165` and `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py:162`,\nwhich asbestos classified non-applicable because a collect-only child never allocates\n`TempPathFactory._basetemp`. The next site added by hand is the fourth instalment.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `tests/_nested_pytest.py` with\n\n    run_nested_pytest(tmp_path, *args, timeout, env, cwd=REPO_ROOT, no_cacheprovider=True)\n        -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]\n\n`env` is REQUIRED and passed through verbatim — it is never merged onto `os.environ` and never\nre-wrapped. Four sites (`test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py:31`, `test_environ_assert_repr_security.py:134`,\n`test_fixture_env_repr_security.py:49`, `test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py:189`) hand the child a\ndeliberately minimal two- or three-key mapping so pytest's bounded mapping repr cannot truncate the\nsentinel away; widening it would leave those oracles green and vacuous. `env` must also survive as a\nplain `dict` — `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py:39` supplies `{\"PATH\": \"test-path\"}`,\nso the helper may not call `SubprocessEnv` methods on it.\n\nThe helper always appends `--basetemp <tmp_path>/<name>`, `-p no:cacheprovider` (suppressible: the\nparity collector does not pass it today), `stdin=DEVNULL`, `capture_output=True`, `text=True`, and\npasses `timeout` to `subprocess.run` as a KEYWORD — `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py:42`\nreads `kwargs[\"timeout\"]` off an intercepted `subprocess.run` and asserts `>= 30`. It returns the\n`CompletedProcess` unmodified (that same file asserts `result is nested_result` at line 51), sets no\n`check`, and lets `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` propagate so `test_repo_isolation_guard.py:105-108` can\nkeep converting it into its own diagnostic.\n\nPer-site divergences stay at the call site as `*args`: `-n 0` (authorship), `-p no:randomly`\n(engine-dir, ci-snapshot), `-p conftest` (repo-isolation guard), `-rs` (external isolation),\n`--collect-only` (parity, git-floor, live-Jira), `--tb=<style>`/`--showlocals` (the four repr-security\nsites), and the per-site `timeout` values 30/90/300/None. `tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:61`\npasses no `cwd` at all and keeps that by passing `cwd=None` explicitly.\n\nTwo sites are OUT of scope by design: `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:154` (bug 291e)\nand `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:92` (bug a371) spawn the bare `pytest` console script\nfrom a cwd outside the repository precisely so the repo root cannot reach `sys.path`. Routing them\nthrough `sys.executable -m pytest` inserts cwd and destroys both reproductions.\n\nGuard: because Black splits every argv list one element per line, the literal `\"-m\", \"pytest\"` does\nnot occur anywhere in `tests/` and a text grep for it is empty on unmodified `main`. The meta-test is\ntherefore an AST scan — it walks every `tests/**/*.py`, finds `subprocess.run`/`Popen` calls whose\nfirst argument is a list literal containing `sys.executable`, `\"-m\"` and `\"pytest\"` in sequence, and\nasserts the only such site is `tests/_nested_pytest.py`, plus exactly one `def run_nested_pytest`\nunder `tests/`. A `# nested-pytest-ok: <reason>` marker on the call line is the escape, as\n`scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` uses. The unquoted string `-m pytest` occurs 23 times in 16 files\nas prose, regex and docstring data (`tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:640,651,652`,\n`tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py:89`, `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:8-13`,\n`tests/module_size_support.py:17`, ten `tests/scripts/**` module docstrings) and is deliberately not\nmatched.\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`, adapted\nfrom `src/rebar` to `tests/` because the owner module is a test helper. This construct has no\ndistinctive single atom that survives formatting, so branch 4 of the rule applies: assert the\nDEFINITION count (exactly one `def run_nested_pytest` under `tests/`) alongside the AST launch-site\nscan described in Approach. The owner module `tests/_nested_pytest.py` is exempt; the escape marker\nis `# nested-pytest-ok: <reason>`; behaviour is pinned only by the existing tests named in Scope.\n\n## Scope\nNew:\n- `tests/_nested_pytest.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_helper.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py` (the AST + definition-count guard)\n\nConverted (14 sites):\n- `tests/_store_isolation.py:33`\n- `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py:25` (gains `--basetemp`)\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py:24`\n- `tests/unit/test_authorship_fixture_maintenance.py:43`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:61`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:839`\n- `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:188`\n- `tests/unit/test_environ_assert_repr_security.py:141`\n- `tests/unit/test_external_isolation.py:63`\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py:54`\n- `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:165` (gains `--basetemp`)\n- `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py:162` (gains `--basetemp`)\n- `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py:82`\n- `tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py:195`\n\nPinning consumers touched by NO assertion edit, but which must be run to prove the conversion:\n- `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py` (intercepts `subprocess.run`; reads\n  `kwargs[\"timeout\"]`, asserts identity of the returned `CompletedProcess`, supplies a plain-dict env)\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity_basetemp.py` (imports `_collect_node_ids` from\n  `test_ci_workflow_parity` by name; pins `PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT` sentinel survival)\n- `tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation.py` and `tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation_heldout.py`\n  (drive `assert_nodes_do_not_mutate_external_store`; depend on `PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT` reaching the child)\n\nExplicitly NOT converted, with the reason recorded in the helper docstring:\n- `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:154` — bare console script, bug 291e\n- `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:92` — bare console script, bug a371\n- the 6 `pytester.runpytest_subprocess` calls in `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` and the\n  4 `pytester.runpytest` calls in `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py:285,305,321,342`, which\n  already receive pytest's own managed basetemp\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: the helper runs a one-test file and returns rc 0 with its basetemp under `tmp_path`.\nEdge: a hanging child raises `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` at `timeout` (no wall-clock assertion; a hang\nguard marked `# timing: hang-guard`), so `test_repo_isolation_guard.py:105` keeps its diagnostic.\nEdge: `timeout` reaches `subprocess.run` as a keyword and the returned object is the identical\n`CompletedProcess`, proven by a probe that intercepts `subprocess.run` the way\n`test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py` does.\nEdge: a caller-supplied plain `dict` env is forwarded byte-identically, with no key added or removed —\nthis is what keeps the four repr-security oracles non-vacuous.\nPinning: the four consumers named in Scope pass with no assertion edits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly one nested-pytest launch site exists under `tests/`: no `tests/**/*.py` other than\n      `tests/_nested_pytest.py` contains a `subprocess.run`/`Popen` call whose argv list literal holds\n      `sys.executable`, `\"-m\"` and `\"pytest\"` in sequence, except on a line carrying a\n      `# nested-pytest-ok: <reason>` marker. Checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py::test_the_nested_pytest_launch_appears_only_in_the_helper`,\n      which is an AST scan and not a text grep — Black splits argv one element per line, so\n      `grep -rn '\"-m\", \"pytest\"' tests/` matches nothing even on unmodified `main` and would pass\n      vacuously.\n- [ ] Exactly one definition of the helper exists. Checked by\n      `grep -rn '^def run_nested_pytest' tests/` returning exactly one line, in `tests/_nested_pytest.py`.\n- [ ] The two bare-console-script launches survive unconverted, because converting them would insert\n      cwd on `sys.path` and void bugs 291e and a371. Checked by\n      `grep -rln 'Path(sys.executable).parent / \"pytest\"' tests/` returning exactly\n      `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py` and `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py`,\n      and by both modules passing unchanged.\n- [ ] Every nested run's basetemp is under the caller's `tmp_path`. Checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_helper.py::test_the_child_basetemp_is_owned_by_the_caller`\n      inspecting the child's `--basetemp`, and by `grep -rln -- '--basetemp' tests/` returning only\n      `tests/_nested_pytest.py`.\n- [ ] A caller-supplied environment mapping reaches the child byte-identically, with no key added and\n      none removed, so the four minimal-env repr-security oracles stay non-vacuous. Checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_helper.py::test_the_caller_environment_is_forwarded_verbatim`\n      and by `tests/unit/test_environ_assert_repr_security.py`,\n      `tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py`, `tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py`,\n      `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py` passing with no assertion edits.\n- [ ] `timeout` reaches `subprocess.run` as a keyword and the helper returns the `CompletedProcess`\n      unmodified. Checked by `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py` passing with no\n      assertion edits (it asserts `kwargs[\"timeout\"] >= 30` and `result is nested_result`).\n- [ ] The per-site divergences are preserved, not normalised: `-n 0`, `-p no:randomly`, `-p conftest`,\n      `-rs`, `--collect-only`, `--tb=<style>`/`--showlocals`, the inherited cwd at\n      `test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`, and the 30/90/300/None timeouts. Checked by\n      `git diff origin/main -- tests/` showing each flag still present at its call site, and by the\n      fourteen converted modules passing with no assertion edits.\n- [ ] The parity collector stays importable by name for its basetemp regression. Checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity_basetemp.py` passing unchanged (it does\n      `from test_ci_workflow_parity import _DEFAULT_SELECTION, _collect_node_ids`).\n- [ ] `PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT` still reaches the store-isolation child, so the\n      `asbestos-popular-tench` regression remains live. Checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation.py::test_nested_pytest_does_not_clean_shared_numbered_temp_root`\n      passing for all three parametrisations.\n- [ ] The converted files pass in the default `Verified` tier — `-n 4 --dist worksteal` on ubuntu and\n      `-n 3` on macOS per `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:657` — plus the\n      `--dist loadgroup` lane at line 672, and the `integration` tier for\n      `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py`. Checked by CI.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit zero.\n\n## Review remediation (2026-08-21)\n- The original AC `grep -rn '\"-m\", \"pytest\"' tests/` returns ZERO hits on unmodified `main` (Black splits argv one element per line), so it passed vacuously; the guard is now an AST scan.\n- Fourteen `sys.executable -m pytest` sites exist, not fifteen; the \"twelve other sites found by `grep -rln`\" were zero files.\n- All three cited bugs are CLOSED (`bf7c-333e-29b0-4ee4`, `444d-62ff-2c3c-42a9`, `fb03-2609-ef83-4b41`), and two of the three files described as \"missing `--basetemp`\" already have it — `tests/_store_isolation.py:41` and `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:848`.\n- The three sites genuinely lacking `--basetemp` are `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py:25`, `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:165` and `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py:162`; the first executes real fixtures and was absent from both the asbestos inventory and the original Scope.\n- `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:154` (bug 291e) and `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:92` (bug a371) launch the BARE `pytest` console script on purpose and must NOT be converted — `sys.executable -m pytest` inserts cwd on `sys.path` and voids both reproductions.\n- Four sites pass a deliberately minimal two/three-key env so pytest's bounded mapping repr cannot truncate the sentinel; the helper must forward `env` verbatim or those oracles go green-but-vacuous.\n- `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py` pins the call contract: `timeout` must be a keyword on `subprocess.run` and stay `>= 30`, the `CompletedProcess` must be returned by identity, and a plain-`dict` env must survive without `SubprocessEnv` method calls."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787368698396809001,"uuid":"3b8b111b-bebc-43ef-a32f-3d594ab9473f"}